  "title": "Quantum reference frame",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "18f9dde8-a478-49de-825e-c2e7d6981409",
      "text": "A quantum reference frame is a physical system, such as a meter stick, clock or gyroscope, that lets measured values be compared and given meaning. It encodes unmeasurable phase information and so cannot be fully specified by any finite bit string.",
